```javascript
import Text from 'react-text'; // Import the Text component from react-text

const WidowRemover = ({ children }) => {
  const styles = {
    whiteSpace: 'nowrap',
    overflow: 'hidden',
    textOverflow: 'ellipsis',
  };

  return (
    <Text>
      <span style={{ ...styles, hyphens: 'auto' }}>{children}</span>
    </Text>
  );
};

export default WidowRemover;
```

3. In this example, we create a new functional component called `WidowRemover`. This component takes one prop, `children`, which is the text content that we want to apply the widow removal logic to. We set the `whiteSpace` property to `nowrap` to prevent line wrapping and the `overflow` and `textOverflow` properties to `hidden` and `ellipsis`, respectively, to ensure that any truncated text is displayed as ellipses. The crucial part is setting the `hyphens` property to `auto`, which allows the browser to automatically insert hyphens at appropriate places to prevent widows.

